    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Part c sets the demand. The student must write (x-2) as a fraction over x+2 and expand (x-2)(x+2) to x^2-4. They must then subtract it with the bracket sign handled correctly, so x^2 cancels to leave 4/(x+2). This is a routine linked procedure with a few more decisions than p34-q9, where the second term already has a squared denominator, so the common denominator is a visible factor. It is easier than p34-q10, whose parts include two unlike linear denominators with a final factorisation, or a multi-term numerator with a squared denominator. Parts a and b are simpler single-step combinations and do not raise the demand.",
